# Build output
package/build/
*.mpackage
svof/

# Per-profile runtime state.
#
# All of this is written into the Mudlet profile directory rather than the repo, so it
# should never appear here at all -- but a checkout placed inside the profile puts them
# side by side, and these files carry character-specific data: kill lists, captured game
# text, tuned thresholds. Matched by prefix so a new state file is covered before anyone
# has to remember to add it.
emunah-*.lua
emunah-*.txt
emunah-*.json

# Mudlet profile artifacts. Map files and profile backups are large, binary, and record the
# character's own exploration history.
*.dat
*.map
AdjustableContainer/
profiles/

# Game logs and transcripts.
#
# The category most worth being careful about: a MUD log is a verbatim record of everything
# on screen, which includes tells, clan and city channels, other players' names, and
# anything mistyped into the input line. Transcripts that establish a mechanic belong in
# docs/game/ as quoted excerpts with their timestamps, never as whole logs.
*.log
logs/
transcripts/
*.txt.gz

# Credentials. Nothing here needs any, which is exactly why this is worth stating -- it is
# cheap insurance against that changing without the ignore file changing with it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*

# Git artifacts that carry history.
#
# A bundle or a patch series contains the commit history it was made from, including any
# history this repository was deliberately published without. Committing one would restore
# in a file exactly what was removed from the log.
*.bundle
*.patch
*.orig
*.rej

# Tooling that stores local session state, prompts or transcripts alongside the code.
.claude/
.aider*
.cursor/
.continue/

# Archives. Usually a snapshot of a working directory, which is how an ignored file ends up
# committed inside something that is not itself ignored.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# Analysis and scratch output
graphify-out/
scratch/
tmp/
*.bak
*~

# Python tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Third-party reference code kept locally for study, not redistributed.
stuff/
